WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.507
Welcome to the Concilium Security Risk Brief for Saturday, November seventh.

2
00:00:04.507 --> 00:00:11.998
Five minutes of security coverage from the last twenty four hours, to increase your situational awareness without decreasing your productivity.

3
00:00:11.998 --> 00:00:14.404
Here's what matters today.

4
00:00:14.404 --> 00:00:33.436
Today: a U.S. heightened vigilance alert for Americans across the Middle East, a new U.K. travel restriction around Moyale on the Kenya Ethiopia border, the rising death toll from the Zaporizhzhia aid point strike, a deadly A D F raid in eastern Congo that disrupted Ebola care, and a Spain wide general strike set for Wednesday.

5
00:00:33.436 --> 00:00:35.054
We start with the Middle East.

6
00:00:35.054 --> 00:00:35.881
The U.S.

7
00:00:35.881 --> 00:00:48.204
State Department says Americans currently in the Middle East should exercise heightened vigilance due to the increased threat of armed attacks by Iranian supported Houthis and Iranian efforts to target U.S. government officials in the region.

8
00:00:48.204 --> 00:00:57.362
TravelGov warns of potential flight cancellations, airspace closures, and travel disruptions, and points travelers to country specific embassy alerts.

9
00:00:57.362 --> 00:00:58.780
Next, Kenya.

10
00:00:58.780 --> 00:00:59.568
The U.K.

11
00:00:59.568 --> 00:01:08.081
Foreign Office now advises against all but essential travel to Moyale Town and up to five kilometers around it, including to the border with Ethiopia.

12
00:01:08.081 --> 00:01:11.332
The page was updated Friday and remains current today.

13
00:01:11.332 --> 00:01:12.756
Turning to Ukraine.

14
00:01:12.756 --> 00:01:23.648
Reuters reports the death toll from Russia's bombing of an aid distribution point in the Zaporizhzhia region on Monday, November second, has risen to fifty three, according to the acting regional governor.

15
00:01:23.648 --> 00:01:26.050
In the Democratic Republic of the Congo.

16
00:01:26.050 --> 00:01:38.020
Reuters reports Islamic State linked Allied Democratic Forces militants attacked Cantine Aloya in North Kivu, burning homes, a health center and other buildings, and killing at least thirty three civilians.

17
00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:43.405
Reuters also reports Islamist militants forced Ebola patients to flee in the deadly raid.

18
00:01:43.405 --> 00:01:49.363
The U.N. humanitarian office says insecurity has disrupted the Ebola response in Beni territory.

19
00:01:49.363 --> 00:01:51.017
And looking ahead in Europe.

20
00:01:51.017 --> 00:01:56.241
The State Department says a general strike is scheduled across Spain on Wednesday, November eleventh.

21
00:01:56.241 --> 00:02:04.985
Workers from all sectors, including hospitality and transportation, are called to strike, and public transportation will be limited to minimum services.

22
00:02:04.985 --> 00:02:08.283
Confirm travel plans with your train company or airline.

23
00:02:08.283 --> 00:02:11.466
Now a few quick notes by region.

24
00:02:11.466 --> 00:02:19.735
In Africa, A C LED reports Ethiopian federal forces moving toward Rama in Tigray, with a nighttime vehicle curfew in Mekele.

25
00:02:19.735 --> 00:02:28.985
In Europe, Reuters reports bomb threats warning that the clock is ticking disrupted television channels across Europe, extending the recent wave of hoax threats beyond aviation.

26
00:02:28.985 --> 00:02:36.939
The State Department also notes continued protests in France, including planned demonstrations in Paris on Saturday.

27
00:02:36.939 --> 00:02:43.122
In the Middle East, Reuters reports a seafarer was killed in a suspected missile attack on a tanker in the Gulf.

28
00:02:43.122 --> 00:02:58.379
In Asia, the Institute for the Study of War assesses that China may be conducting a major, unannounced military exercise simulating surrounding and isolating Taiwan, larger than last year's Justice Mission exercise and involving forces from three coastal theater commands.

29
00:02:58.379 --> 00:02:59.528
On sanctions, the U.S.

30
00:02:59.528 --> 00:03:11.281
Treasury, coordinating with Canada, sanctioned eight Canada based money services businesses for helping the Iranian regime, and FinCEN moved to cut off access for the crypto exchange MEXC Global.

31
00:03:11.281 --> 00:03:23.990
And in cyber, Microsoft Threat Intelligence says a financially motivated group it tracks as Storm thirty three fifty eight is using an agentic A I offensive framework called ARTEX against financial organizations.

32
00:03:23.990 --> 00:03:25.401
That's today's brief.

33
00:03:25.401 --> 00:03:33.462
These security developments come from government travel advisories and trusted analysts, curated by the Concilium Security Risk Management Team.

34
00:03:33.462 --> 00:03:41.671
The brief summarizes public reporting and isn't a substitute for your own risk assessment, so check the original source before making travel decisions.

35
00:03:41.671 --> 00:03:43.743
This brief is digitally narrated.

36
00:03:43.743 --> 00:03:44.665
Questions?

37
00:03:44.665 --> 00:03:48.035
Reach Concilium at info at concilium dot U.S.

38
00:03:48.035 --> 00:03:50.167
Thanks for listening, and stay safe.
